{"kind":"article","metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","title":"FSM Concepts","modules":[{"name":"FSM"}],"role":"article"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FSM\/documentation\/FSM"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Machines","anchor":"Machines","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FSM\/documentation\/FSM\/Machine","type":"reference"},{"text":" represents the structure and behavioural setting","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of a finite state machine, including its transitions, layouts,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and associated boilerpate for the language it is expressed in.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"States","anchor":"States","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The behavioural steps of the system is represented by States."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A state is represented by the "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FSM\/documentation\/FSM\/StateNode"},{"type":"text","text":" concept (protocol)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and implemented by the "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FSM\/documentation\/FSM\/State"},{"type":"text","text":" struct."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The actual behaviour of a state is expressed in a language","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"through a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FSM\/documentation\/FSM\/LanguageBinding","isActive":true},{"text":" implementation in different","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sections of the state.  Sections represent the semantics","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of state behaviour that form ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FSM\/documentation\/FSM\/StateActivities","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"For example, a state in a logic-labelled finite state machine","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"may have an ","type":"text"},{"code":"onEntry","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" section that defines what happens","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"if the state has just been transitioned into.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Transitions","anchor":"Transitions","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FSM\/documentation\/FSM\/Transition","type":"reference"},{"text":" defines how an FSM moves from one state to another.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Each transition has a label, a source state, and a target state.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"In a logic-labelled finite state machine, the label is a Boolean","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"expression that determines whether a transition should fire","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(if the expression evaluates to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"text":") or not.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Languages","anchor":"Languages","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The behaviour of a state machine is expressed in a programming"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"language through a concrete type that conforms to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FSM\/documentation\/FSM\/LanguageBinding"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol.  A language binding that can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be serialised (written to storage) needs to conform to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FSM\/documentation\/FSM\/OutputLanguage"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol."}]},{"text":"Arrangements","anchor":"Arrangements","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A collection of finite state machines can be composed into"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"complex system behaviour through an "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FSM\/documentation\/FSM\/Arrangement","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"In an arrangement, machines can interact and control"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each other, implementing structural concepts such as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the subsumption architecture."}]},{"text":"Serialisation","anchor":"Serialisation","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"FSMs can be serialised to and from various formats","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for persistence and interoperability.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The serialised representation of a machine is captured by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FSM\/documentation\/FSM\/MachineWrapper","isActive":true},{"text":", and the serialised representation","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of an arrangement is captured by an ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FSM\/documentation\/FSM\/ArrangementWrapper","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"This page covers key concepts underpinning the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FSM\/documentation\/FSM\/FSM","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" framework.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/fsm\/concepts"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/FSM\/documentation\/FSM\/Concepts","interfaceLanguage":"swift"}